1
00:02:14,502 --> 00:02:20,887
<v Events Coordinator>Good morning, you’re through to the events coordinator at the Birmingham City ouncil, how may I help you?


2
00:02:20,887 --> 00:02:31,029
<v Julie> Hello there, my husband and I are interested in  Example purchasing tickets to the automobile exhibition, but I couldn’t ﬁnd many details about it on your website,

3
00:02:31,029 --> 00:02:36,948
<v Julie>and  I  was  wondering  whether  you  could  provide  me  with  some  more information. Does it open in June?


4
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:39,000
<v Events Coordinator>Yes, of course, Madam.

5
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:50,977
<v Events Coordinator>The exhibition will take  place during July, and will showcase the history of automobiles from the very ﬁrst  commercial car in the late 1800s all the way through to the present day.


6
00:02:50,977 --> 00:02:54,608
<v Julie>Is the exhibition open for the duration of July?

7
00:02:54,608 --> 00:03:04,923
<v Events Coordinator>No, Madam, the exhibition will last 3 days, from the 1st of July to the 3rd of July, and then the cars will be taken to another exhibition.


8
00:03:04,923 --> 00:03:09,671
<v Julie>Okay. Does the exhibition focus on a certain manufacturer?  

9
00:03:09,671 --> 00:03:14,501
<v Events Coordinator>No, it will showcase a wide range of manufacturers.

10
00:03:14,501 --> 00:03:20,834
<v Julie> Wonderful! I’m ever so fed up of going to these shows and only seeing one manufacturer.

11
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:25,332
 <v Julie>Are there any opportunities to sit in or even drive the cars?


12
00:03:25,332 --> 00:03:32,745
<v Events Coordinator>There will be many opportunities for you to sit in the cars; however, some of the cars will only be available to observe.

13
00:03:32,745 --> 00:03:45,036
<v Events Coordinator>We are yet to be told whether any of the antique cars will be available to drive, however there will certainly be an opportunity to test driving some of the more modern cars on a purpose-built track.


14
00:03:45,036 --> 00:03:51,763
<v Julie>That sounds like great fun! I mustn’t forget to bring my camera, or my husband will never forgive me!

15
00:03:51,763 --> 00:03:57,626
<v Events Coordinator>I’m afraid to say that Q4 cameras are actually strictly not allowed to bring into the exhibition.

16
00:03:57,626 --> 00:04:06,878
<v Events Coordinator>There will however be a section where a professional photographer will be available to take photos of you sitting in a car in period clothing.


17
00:04:06,878 --> 00:04:11,967
<v Julie> Well, that sounds like it could be fun, but I assume the photos won’t be free.


18
00:04:11,967 --> 00:04:20,632
<v Events Coordinator> On the contrary, one free photograph is included within every ticket, but each photo after this will cost £5.


19
00:04:56,163 --> 00:05:00,004
<v Julie>That’s a nice surprise, not many things are free anymore.

20
00:05:00,004 --> 00:05:05,730
<v Julie>I’ve been asking around about the ticket prices, but I haven’t yet had a deﬁnite answer.

21
00:05:05,730 --> 00:05:11,742
<v Julie>Is it correct that the tickets are £100 whether you buy them now or on arrival?


22
00:05:11,742 --> 00:05:20,895
<v Events Coordinator>I’m afraid not. If you buy the ticket in advance the price is £110, but it’s £165 on the door.


23
00:05:20,895 --> 00:05:25,065
<v Julie>Oh goodness! I suppose I’d best pay for them now then.

24
00:05:25,065 --> 00:05:28,971
<v Julie>Is it possible to buy tickets from you now over the phone?


25
00:05:28,971 --> 00:05:35,073
<v Events Coordinator>Yes, of course, Madam. I’ll transfer you to the Box Oﬃce Manager, Mark Edgeworth,

26
00:05:35,073 --> 00:05:47,921
<v Events Coordinator>that’s E-D-G-E-W-O-R-T-H, and he will probably need to take your credit card details and some personal details.


27
00:05:47,921 --> 00:05:54,074
<v Julie>Yes, that’s ﬁne. Before you transfer me, I just need to ask a few more questions.

28
00:05:54,074 --> 00:06:00,816
<v Julie>Will the exhibition be held in the Birmingham Exhibition Centre? I think that’s where I went last time.


29
00:06:00,816 --> 00:06:10,716
<v Events Coordinator> No, Madam, the Birmingham Exhibition Centre is currently undergoing some renovations, so this year all exhibitions will be held in the Summer Palace.


30
00:06:10,716 --> 00:06:15,528
<v Julie>Summer Palace? I’m not entirely sure where that is.

31
00:06:15,528 --> 00:06:17,967
<v Events Coordinator>Well, it’s not too far from city centre.

32
00:06:17,967 --> 00:06:22,870
<v Events Coordinator>Once you’re in the centre, you should be able to ﬁnd signs for the palace.

33
00:06:22,870 --> 00:06:27,248
<v Events Coordinator>If not, most people in Birmingham will be able to direct you.

34
00:06:27,248 --> 00:06:31,680
<v Julie>Hmm...neither my husband nor I am particularly good with directions.

35
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:35,268
<v Julie>Is there anywhere I can find this information on the Internet?


36
00:06:35,268 --> 00:06:38,585
<v Events Coordinator>Our website will give you an address. 

37
00:06:38,585 --> 00:06:49,652
<v Events Coordinator>Perhaps you could visit Q9 www.directions.com for more detailed information, and they should be able to provide you with step-by-step instructions.

38
00:06:49,652 --> 00:06:55,036
<v Julie>Okay and is this the best way to contact you, by phone?


39
00:06:55,036 --> 00:07:05,880
<v Events Coordinator>I think the most convenient way to contact us is enquiring online, which is much simpler than having to dial various diﬀerent numbers to reach the right person!

40
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:09,548
<v Events Coordinator>Unless you have any more questions, I’ll transfer you now.


41
00:07:09,548 --> 00:07:12,781
<v Julie>No, that’s great! Thank you for your help.